Z||000014||Seanh||11-02-2000||11:35 PM||||I will probally do a how to section on things like that. I was going to do it, but then I figured there were enough Fiero sites that explained that well enough, so I didnt put it on my first page. I am working on a new website with the dynamic html and flash videos. I am working on it now, but man, does it take time. I am going to have a page, like some other sites Iv seen, about the stereo system and the installation. I want to wait until I start competing to throw out the spec's of the system, but installation wise, I will include it on my dynamic page. I am thinking about changing out a few things on my system once again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats just me. I have a Polk Momo 10" sub up front now, taking 400 RMS and 720 MAX with a PRS Premier amp, I am thinking of changing to an AudioBahn 10" DVC Compression Piston Sub and give it 1200 RMS and 2000 MAX, with an AudioBahn Mono Amp. Ill be honest, putting Amps in the trunk was the stupidest thing I ever did. I hate it, there is no room for transporting anything and when I work on the engine I like standing in the trunk. The thought has crossed my mind that I should eliminate the subs behind the seat idea, since I havent installed them yet, and put the amps back there. All the amps are two channels amp, some bridged to one chan. I am considering changing and doing this: Keeping the 4" mids in the stock dash locations, keeping the rear 4x6 plates in the stock location and the 6.5 Polk Momo mids in the kickpanels, and the 10" up front with the exception of changind the sub out. Using a 6 channel amp to run the rears, fronts, and kickpanels, and a D class mono subwoofer amp to drive a DVC Compression Piston Subwoofer at 1omh mono. Useing AudioBahn Amps and sub, keeping the Pioneer Rears, and Polk audion mids. This would probally hurt on the SPL competitions, but I didnt really intend to build it for SPL's in the begining. I dont know, I just kinda went off on the subject since it go brought up. Just thought I would share. I will have a stereo page in my new website though.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||11-03-2000||08:43 AM||||instead of Audiobahn just spend the few extra bucks and get an Xtant. they have more / better cooling so you can BEAT the crap out it and never have it flinch. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>   my old car with an Xtant 1001DX w/lfq45 and Kac 626, and Sony CDX-C910. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
